🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch
Now the latest version of Libtorch does not support  real tensor and complex tensor do einsum at the same time.  See the following code:
#include <torch/torch.h>
#include <iostream>
int main()
{
    auto a_real = torch::ones({2, 2});
    auto b_real = torch::randn({2, 2});
    auto b_imag = torch::randn({2, 2});
    auto b = torch::complex(b_real, b_imag);
    auto c = torch::einsum("ij,jk->ik", {a_real, b});
    std::cout << torch::real(c) << std::endl;
    return 0;
}

The code can compile succussfully but run error. The error information is as follows:
terminate called after throwing an instance of 'c10::Error'
  what():  expected scalar type Float but found ComplexFloat
Exception raised from data_ptr<float> at aten/src/ATen/core/TensorMethods.cpp:18 (most recent call first):

And if I change the code as follows to make two complex tensor do einsum.
#include <torch/torch.h>
#include <vector>
#include <iostream>
#include <chrono>
int main()
{
    auto a_real = torch::ones({2, 2});
    auto a_imag = torch::ones({2, 2});
    auto a = torch::complex(a_real, a_imag);
    auto b_real = torch::randn({2, 2});
    auto b_imag = torch::randn({2, 2});
    auto b = torch::complex(b_real, b_imag);
    auto c = torch::einsum("ij,jk->ik", {a, b});
    std::cout << torch::real(c) << std::endl;
    return 0;
}

The above code can run successfully.
Alternatives
Libtorch torch::einsum(...) need support real tensor and complex tensor do einsum.
