🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch
Libtorch (C++ API of pytorch)  dosen't has the function that can set the precision of output number like python api (TORCH.SET_PRINTOPTIONS) .
For example:
torch::Tensor a = torch::randint(0, 5, {2, 2}, torch::kDouble);
auto b = torch::randint(5, 10, {2, 2}, torch::kDouble);
auto c = torch::complex(a, b);
std::cout << "the complex real and img is :" << std::endl;
std::cout << torch::real(c) << std::endl;
std::cout << torch::imag(c) << std::endl;
std::cout << " the abs is : " << std::endl;
std::cout << torch::abs(c) << std::endl;

the out put is as follows:

the abs of complex number is quoted in four decimal places. But I want make the result  quoted in ten decimal places. In current API， I can't do this.
Thanks a lot.
Alternatives
Libtorch provides the api like python api (TORCH.SET_PRINTOPTIONS) in the future.
